#: ../../../guide/performance.md:28
msgid "Memory Traffic and Fusion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:30
msgid ""
"Keep intermediate results in tiles to avoid repeated global-memory access:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:32
msgid ""
"#[cutile::entry()]\n"
"fn fused<const BM: i32, const BN: i32>(\n"
"    z: &mut Tensor<f32, { [BM, BN] }>,\n"
"    x: &Tensor<f32, { [-1, -1] }>,\n"
") {\n"
"    let tile = x.load_like(z);\n"
"    let centered = tile - reduce_max(tile, 1i32)\n"
"        .reshape(shape![BM, 1])\n"
"        .broadcast(shape![BM, BN]);\n"
"    let exp_x = exp(centered);\n"
"    let sum = reduce_sum(exp_x, 1i32)\n"
"        .reshape(shape![BM, 1])\n"
"        .broadcast(shape![BM, BN]);\n"
"    z.store(true_div(exp_x, sum));\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:50
msgid ""
"Kernel fusion applies this pattern across a pipeline. Three unfused kernels "
"often read and write intermediate tensors several times. One fused kernel "
"can keep those intermediates in registers."
msgstr ""

