#: ../../../guide/performance.md:66
msgid "Tensor Cores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:68
msgid ""
"Use `mma` and `mmaf_scaled` for matrix multiply paths. The compiler lowers "
"supported dtype and shape combinations to Tensor Core instructions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:70
msgid ""
"let mut acc = constant(0.0f32, shape![BM, BN]);\n"
"for k_tile in 0i32..k_tiles {\n"
"    let tile_x = part_x.load([pid_m, k_tile]);\n"
"    let tile_y = part_y.load([k_tile, pid_n]);\n"
"    acc = mma(tile_x, tile_y, acc);\n"
"}\n"
"z.store(acc);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:80
msgid ""
"For block-scaled formats such as NVFP4 and MXFP8, `mmaf_scaled` consumes low-"
"precision input tiles plus per-block scale tiles. See [Tutorial 11: "
"Inference with NVFP4/MXFP8](../tutorials/11-nvfp4-inference.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:82
msgid "Bounds and Mapped Partitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:84
msgid ""
"The preferred safe performance path for persistent or mapped traversal is a "
"mapped output partition. The output partition produces bounded, disjoint "
"indices; input partitions are indexed with plain arrays, and the compiler "
"infers the bounds from the loops and mapped components that produce each "
"index:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:86
msgid ""
"fn gemm_persistent<\n"
"    T: ElementType,\n"
"    const BM: i32,\n"
"    const BN: i32,\n"
"    const BK: i32,\n"
"    const MAP_SHAPE: [i32; 2],\n"
">(\n"
"    mut z: MappedPartitionMut<T, { [BM, BN] }, MAP_SHAPE>,\n"
"    x: &Tensor<T, { [-1, -1] }>,\n"
"    y: &Tensor<T, { [-1, -1] }>,\n"
") {\n"
"    let part_x = x.partition(shape![BM, BK]);\n"
"    let part_y = y.partition(shape![BK, BN]);\n"
"\n"
"    for out_idx in z.iter_indices() {\n"
"        let (bid_m, bid_n) = out_idx.components();\n"
"        let mut acc: Tile<T, { [BM, BN] }> = constant(T::ZERO, shape![BM, "
"BN]);\n"
"        for k_tile in 0i32..num_tiles(&part_x, 1) {\n"
"            acc = mma(part_x.load([bid_m, k_tile]), part_y.load([k_tile, "
"bid_n]), acc);\n"
"        }\n"
"        z.store(acc, out_idx);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:112
msgid ""
"`with_bounds(...)`, `Dim::new(...)`, and `coord(...)` are deprecated since "
"0.3.0; [Bounds-Check Placement](bounds-check-placement.md) describes where "
"the remaining checks are placed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:114
msgid ""
"`unchecked_accesses = true` remains available when the programmer wants to "
"opt out of runtime bounds checks explicitly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:116
msgid ""
"#[cutile::entry(unchecked_accesses = true)]\n"
"unsafe fn fast_kernel<const S: [i32; 2]>(...) {\n"
"    // The caller must guarantee every access is in bounds.\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:123
msgid ""
"Use the unsafe path only when the launch shape and tensor sizes are "
"guaranteed by surrounding code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:125
msgid "Compile-Time Hints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:127
msgid "Optimization hints guide code generation for a target architecture:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:129
msgid ""
"#[cutile::entry(\n"
"    optimization_hints = (\n"
"        sm_120 = (\n"
"            num_cta_in_cga = 2,\n"
"            occupancy = 2,\n"
"            max_divisibility = 16,\n"
"            num_worker_warps_per_cta = 4, // Bytecode 13.3+; valid values: "
"1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32.\n"
"        ),\n"
"        sm_90 = (num_cta_in_cga = 1),\n"
"    )\n"
")]\n"
"fn kernel<const S: [i32; 2]>(...) { ... }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:144
msgid ""
"Runtime `CompileOptions` can override entry-level hints, which makes them a "
"tunable axis: put the candidate values in a `Config` and apply them in the "
"tuner's setup closure (see [Autotuning](autotuning.md)). `occupancy`, "
"`num_cta_in_cga`, and `num_worker_warps_per_cta` are architecture-specific "
"scheduling hints; `max_divisibility` controls divisibility assumptions used "
"by the compiler. `num_worker_warps_per_cta` accepts powers of two in the "
"inclusive range `[1, 32]` and requires bytecode version 13.3 or newer. "
"Because compile options are part of the JIT cache key, benchmark a small set "
"of candidates instead of generating many one-off specializations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:146
msgid "Common Pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:148
msgid "Tile shape too small: overhead dominates useful work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:149
msgid ""
"Tile shape too large: register pressure lowers occupancy or causes spills."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:150
msgid ""
"Wrong dtype: using `f32` when `f16`, `bf16`, FP8, or block-scaled formats "
"are acceptable can leave Tensor Core throughput unused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:151
msgid ""
"Excessive synchronization: `.sync()` after every operation creates CPU/GPU "
"gaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:152
msgid "Unfused pipeline: intermediate tensors add global memory traffic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:153
msgid ""
"Strided access pattern: tile loads coalesce well, but algorithmic strides "
"can still reduce effective bandwidth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:155
msgid ""
"Profile before and after each change. [Debugging and Profiling](debugging-"
"and-profiling.md) describes Nsight Compute and Nsight Systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:157
msgid "Measuring Kernels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:159
msgid ""
"`cutile::bench` provides device-event timing for kernel measurement and A/B "
"comparison:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:161
msgid ""
"use cutile::bench::{do_bench, do_bench_paired, BenchOptions};\n"
"\n"
"let r = do_bench(&stream, &BenchOptions::default(), |s| {\n"
"    my_kernel(z.partition([128]), x.clone(), y.clone()).sync_on(s).map(|_| "
"()).map_err(Into::into)\n"
"})?;\n"
"println!(\"median {:.3} ms over {} reps\", r.median_ms(), r.reps());\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:170
msgid ""
"Timing uses CUDA events (device timeline, not host clocks), warmup absorbs "
"first-launch JIT, the L2 cache is cleared between reps, and results report "
"medians and quantiles. When comparing two configurations, use "
"`do_bench_paired`. It alternates the arms rep by rep, so clock and thermal "
"drift cannot masquerade as a difference between them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:172
msgid "Autotuning (experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:174
msgid ""
"`cutile::tune` measures candidate configurations and saves the trials and "
"winning configuration. It requires the `experimental-tune` Cargo feature; "
"see [Autotuning](autotuning.md) for the API. This example searches block "
"sizes for an RMS normalization kernel:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/performance.md:179
msgid ""
"cargo run -p cutile-examples --example autotune --features experimental-"
"tune\n"
msgstr ""

